{\rtf1\ansi\deff0 {\fonttbl {\f0 Times New Roman;}} \f0\fs24\qc \b \fs48 SECURE CLOUD BASED FILE ENCRYPTION \b0 \fs24 \par \par\qc \i A Main Project Report \i0 \par\qc \b Bachelor of Technology \b0 \par\qc \i in \i0 \par\qc \b Computer Science and Engineering \par (Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning) \b0 \par \par\qc \b By \b0 \par\qc VEERAPANI ANJALI (22HU1A42B0) \par\qc PILLI MERI GNANA KUSUMANJALI (22HU1A4266) \par\qc POLURI MOUNIKA (22HU1A4268) \par\qc MANDAPATI ASHOK KUMAR (22HU1A4248) \par\qc NAGA SAI BOPPANA (22HU1A4212) \par \par\qc \b Under the Esteemed Guidance of \b0 \par\qc \b DR. G. BHARATHI \b0 \par\qc \i Associate Professor \i0 \par \par \par\qc \b DEPARTMENT OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGINEERING \parCHEBROLU ENGINEERING COLLEGE (UGC-AUTONOMOUS) \b0 \par\page\qc \b \fs36 ABSTRACT \b0 \fs24 \par \par\qj The increasing reliance on cloud storage services has raised significant concerns regarding data confidentiality, integrity, and unauthorized access. To address these challenges, this work presents a secure cloud-based file encryption system designed to protect sensitive user data before it is uploaded to remote servers. \par \par\qj The system employs strong cryptographic algorithms, such as AES and RSA, to ensure end-to-end security by encrypting files locally on the user's device and allowing only authenticated users to decrypt them. \par}